pyOneNote is used as a dependency and is NOT redistributed here. It is, however,
MODIFIED AT IMPORT TIME: `onenote2md.extract._patch_module` rewrites its
source in memory before executing it. Apache-2.0 section 4(b) asks that changes
be stated, so they are listed here and each carries its reasoning in the source,
in `_PATCHES` and `_DOC_PATCHES`.

Changes made to pyOneNote 0.0.2:

  1. ArrayOfPropertyValues (property type 0x10) raises NotImplementedError
     upstream. Implemented per MS-ONE 2.6.10. The adjacent 0x11 branch calls a
     five-argument constructor with one argument; fixed alongside.
  2. Descending into child nodes assumes every node type set `self.data` with a
     `.ref`. Three do not. The subtree is skipped instead of raising.
  3. A file-data reference is followed without checking it. `isFcrNil()` is
     defined upstream and never called; it is now, plus a bounds check.
  4. `get_compact_ids(count)` trusts a count read from the file. Bounded by the
     number of ids the stream actually holds.
  5. An object declaration seeks to its own `ref` unchecked. Bounded, and a
     failed parse is contained to that object.
  6. `ObjectSpaceObjectStreamOfIDs.Count` bounded: each CompactID is four bytes,
     so the count cannot exceed the bytes remaining.
  7. `FileDataStoreObject.cbLength` bounded by the size its chunk declares.
  8. Rendering a CompactID assumes its index is in the revision's id table. It
     degrades to a marker instead of raising KeyError.
  9. `PrtFourBytesOfLengthFollowedByData.cb` bounded by the file size.
 10. FileNodeListFragment magic (0xA4567AB1F5F7F4C4) is read upstream and never
     compared. It is now, and references are bounded to the file.
 11. Text in a four-bytes-of-length property is decoded as UTF-16 with .hex() as
     the fallback. Single-byte text of odd length cannot be UTF-16, so real text
     became a hex dump. UTF-8 is tried first.
 12. `_files[guid]["identity"]` keeps only the last identity a blob was declared
     under, losing every page that referenced an earlier one. All are kept.

Additionally, unrecognised jcids are reported with their number rather than all
being labelled "Unknown", which is what makes ink identifiable.
